@comment  node-name,  next,  previous,  up
@section Element Rank Mixin
@cindex Element Rank Mixin

Ranked elements are objects that know their position within a flexichain. This is useful for applications like text editors where elements need to track their location.

@deftp {Abstract Class} <element-rank-mixin>
A mixin class that provides rank (position) awareness to elements.

@table @var
@item index
Internal index within the flexichain (managed automatically)
@item chain
Reference to the containing flexichain
@end table

@lisp
(module example-ranked-element (library flexichain))

;; Define a ranked element type
(define-class <text-element>::<element-rank-mixin>
   content::string)

;; Create elements
(define elem1 (instantiate::<text-element> 
                (content "hello")
                (index 0)
                (chain ranked-chain)))
@end lisp
@end deftp

@subsection Rank Operations

@deffn {Generic Function} rank element
Returns the current position of @var{element} within its flexichain.

@lisp
(module example-rank (library flexichain))

(rank elem1) ; => 0 (first position)
@end lisp
@end deffn

@deffn {Generic Function} flexi-first? element
Returns @code{#t} if @var{element} is at the first position in its flexichain.

@lisp
(flexi-first? elem1) ; => #t
@end lisp
@end deffn

@deffn {Generic Function} flexi-last? element
Returns @code{#t} if @var{element} is at the last position in its flexichain.

@lisp
(flexi-last? elem1) ; => #f (assuming more elements exist)
@end lisp
@end deffn

@subsection Navigation Methods

@deffn {Generic Function} flexi-next element
Returns the element immediately after @var{element} in the flexichain. Raises an error if @var{element} is the last element.

@lisp
(define next-elem (flexi-next elem1))
@end lisp
@end deffn

@deffn {Generic Function} flexi-prev element
Returns the element immediately before @var{element} in the flexichain. Raises an error if @var{element} is the first element.

@lisp
(define prev-elem (flexi-prev elem2))
@end lisp
@end deffn

@node Ranked Gapbuffer, Navigation Methods, Element Rank Mixin, Ranked Elements
@comment  node-name,  next,  previous,  up
@section Ranked Gapbuffer
@cindex Ranked Gapbuffer

@deftp {Class} <ranked-gapbuffer>
A specialized gapbuffer that automatically manages element ranks when elements implement the @code{<element-rank-mixin>}.
@end deftp

@deffn {Function} make-ranked-gapbuffer @t{#!key} (initial-capacity 0) (fill #\_) (min-capacity 5) (expand-factor 1.5)
Creates a new ranked gapbuffer that automatically updates element positions.

@lisp
(define ranked-chain (make-ranked-gapbuffer))
@end lisp
@end deffn

@subsection Automatic Rank Management

When elements that implement @code{<element-rank-mixin>} are inserted into or removed from a ranked gapbuffer, their rank information is automatically updated:

@lisp
;; Create a ranked chain
(define chain (make-ranked-gapbuffer))

;; Create ranked elements
(define elem1 (instantiate::<text-element> 
                (content "first")
                (index 0)
                (chain chain)))
(define elem2 (instantiate::<text-element> 
                (content "second")
                (index 1)
                (chain chain)))

;; Insert elements
(flexi-insert! chain 0 elem1)
(flexi-insert! chain 1 elem2)

;; Ranks are automatically maintained
(rank elem1) ; => 0
(rank elem2) ; => 1

;; Insert between them
(define elem-middle (instantiate::<text-element> 
                      (content "middle")
                      (index 1)
                      (chain chain)))
(flexi-insert! chain 1 elem-middle)

;; All ranks are automatically updated
(rank elem1)       ; => 0
(rank elem-middle) ; => 1  
(rank elem2)       ; => 2
@end lisp

@node Navigation Methods, , Ranked Gapbuffer, Ranked Elements
@comment  node-name,  next,  previous,  up
@section Navigation Methods
@cindex Navigation Methods

Ranked elements provide convenient navigation methods that work directly with the element objects rather than positions.

@subsection Example Usage

@lisp
;; Create a document with ranked paragraphs
(define-class <paragraph>::<element-rank-mixin>
   text::string)

(define doc (make-ranked-gapbuffer))

(define para1 (instantiate::<paragraph> 
                (text "First paragraph")
                (index 0)
                (chain doc)))
(define para2 (instantiate::<paragraph> 
                (text "Second paragraph")
                (index 1)
                (chain doc)))
(define para3 (instantiate::<paragraph> 
                (text "Third paragraph")
                (index 2)
                (chain doc)))

(flexi-insert! doc 0 para1)
(flexi-insert! doc 1 para2)
(flexi-insert! doc 2 para3)

;; Navigate through paragraphs
(define current para2)
(define prev-para (flexi-prev current))  ; => para1
(define next-para (flexi-next current))  ; => para3

;; Check positions
(flexi-first? para1) ; => #t
(flexi-last? para3)  ; => #t
(rank para2)         ; => 1
@end lisp

@subsection Performance Considerations

Ranked elements provide O(1) navigation between adjacent elements, making them very efficient for sequential access patterns common in text processing and document manipulation applications.
